From 4a44598b65073a495be2347570b24c17535beac9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:58:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc: the long-term store is one pinned USB volume

Field (RT-BE86U, one SSD, two partitions): both partitions grew .reaper/ and
reaper/, and the traffic history was split between them, because three
resolvers each took "the first mounted volume" and the mount order changes
per boot. The store is now a pinned volume (reaper_store_vid/vname): the
watchdog adopts one on the upgrade path - the volume that holds the history,
the most recently written when both do, after the box has settled - and keeps
a last-seen stamp while it is mounted. A missing pinned volume is waited for
(RAM meanwhile), never replaced by another. The Storage page lists the mounted
volumes, the pin and its state; store_set takes vol=.

The httpd side (store_status / store_set, rdev_store_base) and the two
defaults rows ride the security-review commit with the rest of web.c and
defaults.c; rtrafd's reaper_store.h include rides the rtrafd commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
